{#
    A heading, and the way to hand somebody the place it names.

    The core writes the heading alone and puts the id on the section around it,
    so every heading on a page is a target nothing can point at. The mark is
    the one `sds-confval` already draws beside a name — same glyph, same
    behaviour — under the document layer's own class, so a page has one idiom
    for "link to this" rather than two.

    Not on the page title: a link to the top of a page is the address the
    reader is already holding.
#}
<h{{ node.level }}{% if node.classes %} class="{{ node.classesString }}"{% endif %}>
    {{- renderNode(node.value) -}}
    {%- if node.level > 1 and node.id %}<a class="sds-permalink" href="#{{ node.id }}" aria-label="Permalink to {{ node.toString }}">#</a>{% endif -%}
</h{{ node.level }}>
